(854, 1732, 'MarvinFeari', 'dapu10@imhotester.forum', 'https://freecoloranalysis.org', '186.65.117.55', '2026-04-17 08:42:47', '2026-04-17 08:42:47', '\"spintax_text\": \"I have recently been looking into different color palettes and found that figuring out your season can really help when choosing clothes or makeup. For example, if you have a deep summer color season or are identifying with the soft winter palette, knowing this can point you to colors that flatter fair olive skin or red undertone skin perfectly. There are some fantastic tools like the Color Analysis Pro app and free color analysis quizzes online that support this, including a handy skin tone chart to discover where you belong in the 16 season color analysis test. \r\n \r\nIf you\'ve experimented with the Color Analysis Pro service but need to cancel, it\'s useful to know exactly how to cancel your subscription to avoid surprise billing (you can find detailed steps here  [url=https://freecoloranalysis.org]what season am i[/url] ). Also, for those questioning \"what season am I?\" or \"what is my color palette?\" zeroing in on palettes such as deep summer, soft winter, or even the dark summer color palette can truly define your best colors. This can be remarkably effective for determining the best colors for pale olive skin or yellow undertone skin, making styling decisions far simpler.\"', 0, '0', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/129.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', 'comment', 0, 0),
